 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "notice",
   "text": "Draft for Jared's approval. Collected word for word from the city-wide rules paragraphs of the neighbourhood guides listed at the bottom (D-202); nothing new was added. Each guide keeps what is specific to it and links here.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Buying anywhere in Pitt Meadows? These are the rules that apply city-wide, by topic: property taxes, transfer tax and GST, floodplain, farmland and environmental rules, strata, co-op and age rules and zoning, suites and small-scale housing. The neighbourhood guides cover what is specific to each area. Rules change, so check anything that matters for your purchase with the City of Pitt Meadows and your lawyer before you remove subjects.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Property taxes, transfer tax and GST in Pitt Meadows",
   "id": "taxes",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Property taxes — read the bill by class: under the 2026 Annual Tax Rates Bylaw No. 3047, 2026 (adopted May 5, 2026), the Farm class (Class 9) general rate is $48.6824 per $1,000 with a $1.8524 drainage levy, versus Class 1 Residential at $2.8438 general and $0.1082 drainage — confirm the property's BC Assessment class before quoting carrying costs on any farm parcel. Taxes were due July 2, 2026, with a 5% penalty after July 2, 2026 and a further 5% after August 1, 2026."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Floodplain, farmland and environmental rules in Pitt Meadows",
   "id": "flood",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "City zoning/OCP: Pitt Meadows Zoning Bylaw No. 2505, 2011 — A-1 General Agricultural min lot 8 ha (one farm house to 500 m² GFA); A-2 min 16 ha; RR-2 4 ha, RR-3 2 ha, RR-4 1 ha (RR = land outside the ALR); RS Large Lot Residential min 0.2 ha. One garden suite per lot (33–90 m²) in A-1/A-2/RR-1–RR-5/RS zones (garden suite OR secondary suite, not both); on ALR land the ALC allows one additional detached residence to 90 m² on ≤40 ha where conditions are met, without an application. Buildings in A-1/A-2 sited 15 m from watercourses/key ditches. OCP: \"I See Pitt Meadows 2040\"; North Lougheed Area Plan adopted by OCP Amendment Bylaw No. 3060, 2026 (~50 ha, gradual development, further approvals required)."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Flood / ALR: The city is almost entirely protected by 60 km of dikes; the northern drainage areas (Alouette Pump Station catchment, Fenton, and the Pitt Polder catchment) are drained by floodboxes and pump stations because of low elevation, and the Codd Island Wetlands are undiked floodplain wetlands; 78% of the city's land falls within the Agricultural Land Reserve per the same Business Plan, with property-level ALR status confirmed per address."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Strata, co-op and age rules in Pitt Meadows",
   "id": "strata",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Rental-restriction bylaws are void — and Pitt Meadows separately prohibits short-term rentals city-wide: Since November 24, 2022 (Bill 44), no strata may enforce a long-term rental-restriction bylaw. The voiding does not create a short-term-rental right here: short-term rental accommodation is not a permitted use under the City of Pitt Meadows Zoning Bylaw — a City staff report to Council (October 23, 2024) states this expressly — and the Province's principal-residence requirement also lists Pitt Meadows."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Zoning, suites and small-scale housing in Pitt Meadows",
   "id": "zoning",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Suites and SSMUH: one secondary suite per principal dwelling unit, 33 to 90 sq m, inside the same building, where the zone permits it; garden suites are one per lot at 33 to 90 sq m in the zones listed in the City garden suite guide, and a lot with a garden suite cannot also have a secondary suite. SSMUH unit counts of 3, 4 or 6 turn on the 280 sq m lot-size threshold and the 400 m frequent-transit test; the City's OCP Amendment Bylaw No. 3034, 2025 covers 2–6 units through secondary suites, garden suites, duplexes, triplexes, townhomes and small apartment buildings."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "SSMUH (Pitt Meadows' own position): Duplexes are the baseline two-unit form where SSMUH applies; whether a given lot qualifies is per-parcel."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
